## Question

State the security boundary or behavior under investigation.

## Environment and method

Give exact versions and conditions. Distinguish a proposed experiment from one
actually executed. Use synthetic records and documentation addresses.

```text
Illustrative domain: lab.example.com
Illustrative address: 192.0.2.10
```

## Reproduction steps

Give an ordered procedure, prerequisites and expected observations. Explain how
to distinguish a security decision from a broken setup. If this is only a
proposed procedure, keep that status explicit and do not invent terminal output.

## Evidence and interpretation

Present observed results only when supported by retained evidence. Label
inferences and untested procedures explicitly.

## Remediation and retest

Explain the fix, repeat the original case and retain a permitted control case.

## Limitations

Describe missing coverage, failed attempts and alternative explanations.

## References

Link primary sources beside the claims they support. Attribute upstream work and
state what, if anything, this article independently tested.
